# The unit suite, but deliberately NOT the E2E suite.
#
# `pnpm test` is ~1s, needs no database, no docker and no build, and runs the
# whole suite regardless of what is staged — so there is no partial-check hole
# and nothing to wait for. `pnpm e2e` needs docker compose up, a migrated and
# seeded database and a production build of both apps: ~2.5 minutes when the
# stack happens to be up, and a guaranteed failure when it is not. Wiring that
# into a commit teaches you to reach for `--no-verify`, which would disable the
# checks above along with it. E2E gates on the PR instead (.github/workflows/ci.yml).
pnpm test
